]}},{"id":"investor-wedge","type":"section.wedge","order":3,"props":{"railLabel":"Plan","anchorId":"wedge","showSection":true,"wedgeEyebrow":"How we grow","wedgeTitle":"Start free.\nStay because it works.","wedgeSupport":"Engineers install Nucleify because it removes rewrite pain.\nOnce the product lives in the nucleus, switching away means rewriting the business - then paid work can follow usage.","items":[{"phase":"Land","icon":"mdi:download-outline","title":"People install it themselves","body":"Engineers pull Nucleify because it kills rewrite work - not because a salesperson booked a demo.","signal":"Low cost to start"},{"phase":"Stick","icon":"mdi:lock-outline","title":"Leaving gets expensive","body":"Once domain logic lives in the nucleus, ripping it out means rewriting the business. That stickiness comes from architecture, not contracts.","signal":"Hard to rip out"},{"phase":"Expand","icon":"mdi:expand-all-outline","title":"More stacks, same team","body":"Each new framework is more market reach, not another platform team. Nuxt today, Next or Solid tomorrow - same shared base.","signal":"Reach without headcount"},{"phase":"Earn","icon":"mdi:cash-multiple","title":"Paid work follows usage","body":"Convert and consulting attach after the nucleus is already in production. High intent, shorter sales cycle.","signal":"Money after install"}]}},{"id":"investor-surface","type":"section.surface","order":4,"props":{"railLabel":"Reach","anchorId":"surface","showSection":true,"showStage":true,"surfaceEyebrow":"Where we win","surfaceTitle":"One product. Four ways it reaches the market.","surfaceSupport":"Same shared modules. Different buyers, partners, timing, and paid add-ons - without hiring a second platform team for every framework.","surfaceTabsLabel":"Market reach","surfaceStageLabel":"Reach detail","items":[{"id":"beachhead","index":"01","icon":"mdi:office-building-outline","color":"#00dc82","title":"Teams already paying twice","description":"Product teams stuck on 